WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.410
The highly anticipated second trailer for
Captain Marvel gave fans a closer look at

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:09.639
Brie Larson as Carol Danvers and her fabulous,
occasionally mohawked superhero alter-ego

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:14.579
Captain Marvel, even more eyepatch-less Nick
Fury, and teased an awesome-looking space

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.579
battle sequence.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.540
There was a lot to love in the newest sneak
peek - but one clip does a bit more heavy

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.540
lifting than the rest, solving a minor MCU
mystery.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.660
We know that Captain Marvel tells Carol Danvers'
origin story, and to do that without making

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.340
even more of a mess out of the existing Marvel
Cinematic Universe timeline, directors Anna

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.800
Fleck and Ryan Boden are rolling the clock
back 23 years and introducing the hero in

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.300
1995.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.820
It's an exciting choice, but it was also somewhat
confusing, since Carol Danvers is also lined

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.160
up to appear in Avengers 4, which is set in
the here and now.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.140
If Captain Marvel is set more than 20 years
prior to the events of the Infinity War sequel,

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.700
wouldn't that mean she would be middle-aged
by the time she shows up in the forthcoming

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.200
film?

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.960
And if she isn't pushing 50 in Avengers 4
and does appear in the film in the same youthful

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.550
form that she does in her solo movie, which
is the most likely outcome, does that signal

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.820
time travel is to thank for her involvement?

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.220
That doesn't appear to be the case.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.940
The newest trailer appears to reveal the real
reason for Carol's perpetually youthful appearance:

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.400
it's the result of the accident that left
her human body imbued with DNA from the alien

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.810
race known as the Kree, first introduced in
the MCU in Agents of SHIELD and Guardians

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:24.520
of the Galaxy.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.700
In the trailer, we see Annette Bening appear
as an unnamed, mystery character who explains

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.030
to Carol her Kree origins, telling her that
the Kree rescued her when she was in trouble

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.860
and couldn't remember who she was.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.660
"We made you one of us.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.500
So you could live longer, stronger, superior."

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:48.040
To the average watcher, those lines might
not hold much weight.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.940
Yeah, of course Captain Marvel is physically
powerful and superior to humans whose DNA

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:54.800
isn't comprised of half Kree genetics!

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.060
That's the kind of stuff that makes superheroes
superheroes!

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:03.100
But this clip implies that Carol will outlive
regular humans and will age at a significantly

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:07.710
slower rate, perhaps explaining why she will
barely have gotten any older between the time

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.600
of her accident in Captain Marvel and when
she heads back to Earth in Avengers 4.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.780
Marvel diehards probably already knew all
of this - Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D., for just

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.600
one example, addresses the phenomenal longevity
of the Kree - but more casual Marvel moviegoers

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.780
were likely confused before this revelation.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:27.460
Someone who will feel the effects of time,
however, is Nick Fury.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:33.160
Marvel digitally de-aged Samuel L. Jackson's
character for the entirety of Captain Marvel,

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.660
but he'll be his old self again - literally!
- in time for Avengers 4.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.280
By the time Nick pages Carol for back-up in
the post-credits scene in Infinity War, he's

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.240
sporting some wrinkles and his signature patch
over his eye.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.560
Even with this plot hole-clearing, there's
still much about Captain Marvel fans have

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.560
yet to discover.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.680
Like, what's up with "Goose" the cat?

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.680
Is Pulp Fiction available at that Blockbuster,
making this a Last Action Hero situation?

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:57.680
"No!

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.420
It isn't possible!"

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.000
"What's not possible?

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.360
He's fantastic!"

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.800
Who is Annette Bening playing, and will she
ever run into Michael Douglas in the MCU,

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.280
giving American President fans the reunion
they crave?

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:14.080
Does Carol smack down any other suspicious
septuagenarians, or just subway lady?

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.520
So many questions!

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.880
The good news is that fans won't have to wait
too much longer for answers.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.480
Captain Marvel soars into theaters on March
8th, 2019.

